{
  "$comment": "NPC appearance sets (WORK_QUEUE item 38, BUGS.md #151; owner, 2026-11-13: \"a collection of skin tone ranges with hair color ranges so it's not completely random. Also, face should always match arms\"). `hair`: the hair colours by name (sRGB #rrggbb, a ramp's base). A set (`sets`, named; an NPC's `appearance.set` in creatures.json names one): its skin `tones`, light to deep, each a `name`, a `base` (#rrggbb: the colour every skin vertex of the NPC is drawn in, at its shade), an optional `weight` (default 1) and the `hair` colours that go with it (`colour`: a name in `hair`, `weight`); and `shade` (0..1): how much of the model's own shading inside the skin part (the neck and jaw modelled a ramp darker) the tone keeps, so the face, neck, arms and hands read as one skin. An NPC picks a tone by weight from its variant seed, then a hair colour from that tone's list (dwell-sim `npc_colours`). Clothes keep their own colours (creatures.json `colours`). Prototype content (ARCHITECTURE.md §6.1). Run `node shared/creatures/gen.mjs` after editing.",
